WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.167
-After Tesla and SpaceX
C.E.O. Elon Musk's

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:07.133
acquisition of Twitter, one of
the big political questions

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.434
looming over the platform is

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.167
whether Donald Trump
will get his account back.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.467
Meanwhile, progressives
are sounding the alarm

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:15.067
about billionaire control
of media and big-tech companies.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:17.067
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.267
♪♪

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:23.167
I'm guessing by now
most of you have heard the news

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.167
about Twitter,
unless you're not on Twitter,

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.567
in which case congratulations
on having a life,

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:30.100
because Twitter has stolen mine.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.801
Do you guys remember
when Twitter started

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.834
and the big complaint was people
posting pictures of their food?

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:39.300
Just remember, it can
always get worse than food.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.267
It's like when your Aunt goes on
forever about

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.367
her favorite restaurant, and
you think, "This story sucks,"

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:44.667
and then your
uncle starts talking about

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:45.934
how tough white people have it

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.834
and you realize you miss
the restaurant story.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.334
In fact,
when it comes to Twitter,

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.367
I wish I had the same
approach to posting

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:54.734
that actor Michael Caine has.

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:56.868
On Monday, he tweeted
out of nowhere,

00:00:56.868 --> 00:01:00.868
after several months of silence,
"Hello!"

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:02.667
And then almost immediately
followed that up

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:05.567
with a second tweet that said,
"Good Night My Sweet Ones."

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.067
And hasn't tweeted since.

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:12.234
He popped in,
took one look around,

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.534
and then he just
got the hell out of there.

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:17.133
I imagine that Michael Caine
checking out what was going on

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.734
with Twitter
looked a lot like this.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.901
-Go.
[ Explosion ]

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:26.000
[ Clattering ]

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.634
-[ British accent ]
"Elon, you were only supposed

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:31.000
to blow the bloody doors off."

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:35.133
[ Normally ] We asked ourselves,
"Can we shoehorn

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:37.267
a Michael Caine impression
into 'A Closer Look' today?"

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.767
And the answer was,
"Yes, we Caine."

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:42.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.901
Among the many questions
now looming over Twitter

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.834
after Musk's acquisition
of the company

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:49.067
is whether Donald Trump,
who used his Twitter account

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.133
to foment coups,
direct harassment,

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:54.334
disseminate dangerous lies,
disinformation and racism,

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:55.767
will get his account back.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:58.501
For his part, Trump himself
has said

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:01.167
that even if he's allowed
to return, he won't.

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.601
-Ever since Elon Musk first
raised the prospect

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.234
a couple weeks ago
that he might buy Twitter,

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:07.701
speculation has swirled that,
among other things,

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:10.234
this could result in the
former president, Donald Trump,

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.534
rejoining the social-media site.

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.534
Trump, of course,
was banned from Twitter

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.968
January of last year

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.534
for using the site

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:19.701
to try to foment a violent
insurrection

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:21.367
to overthrow
the U.S. government.

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:24.801
In response to the speculation
that he might be reinstated

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:28.834
to the platform, under an Elon
Musk-owned version of Twitter,

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.968
Trump himself
has reportedly said

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:33.667
that he won't rejoin Twitter,
even if he's allowed to.

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:36.567
-I'm sorry, but there's no way
Trump won't immediately

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.400
go back to tweeting
if he's given the chance.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.067
He'll go back to tweeting with
the same energy

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:41.667
Marty McFly
went back to the future,

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:44.567
which makes sense
because compared to Twitter,

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:47.367
Truth Social
feels like kissing your mom.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.334
And I think that joke really
illustrates the...

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.767
-♪ Power of love ♪

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:52.934
-Can you feel it?

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:54.968
Plus, Trump doesn't have
the self-restraint

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:55.801
to stay off Twitter.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:56.934
Offering him his Twitter back

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:58.901
is like offering
Keith Richards a cigarette.

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:02.667
"Yeah, I'm already smoking one,
but alright.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:05.000
I guess that's what
these two fingers are for."

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:09.334
Twitter was Trump's lifeblood.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.601
He once called himself
the Ernest Hemingway of Twitter.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.300
And according to Politico,
he used to marvel

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.767
at how quickly his tweets
appear on the television screen.

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:21.133
He's like a cat in a science
experiment who figures out,

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.234
if he rings the bell,
he gets a treat.

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:25.601
[ Bell jingles ]

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:27.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.100
"Ring the bell, get a treat.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.033
It's one of the best deals
I've ever made.

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:34.868
It's -- 'Cause ringing the bell,
it costs me nothing. So easy.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.968
And the treat, let me tell you
about the treats.

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:38.501
There's tuna.

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:40.200
There's tuna,
and there's chicken."

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:42.834
And let me just say
for the record

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:44.501
that while banning Trump
from Twitter

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:47.667
has always been complicated,
I think it would be terrible,

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.634
certainly for me,
if Trump got his Twitter back.

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:51.667
Mainly, not having him on
Twitter has just been

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:54.300
a huge
quality-of-life improvement.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.300
Although I will admit,
there have been times when,

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.167
against my better instincts,
I have wondered

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.968
what Trump would have tweeted
during big-news stories,

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:02.667
less for the awful opinions

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:04.834
and more for the weird grammar
and punctuation.

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:06.734
Like, can you imagine
what he would have said

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:08.267
about Will Smith at the Oscars?

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:22.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:24.000
But Trump claims

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.901
he still wants to steer people

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.601
toward his dumb
social media platform,

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.400
which has had a rocky roll-out,

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.667
including bugs and glitches

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:33.334
that have made it difficult
for people to join.

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:36.000
And it can't help that Trump
himself seems incapable

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.167
of remembering
or even pronouncing

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:41.734
the name of his own site,
which is called Truth Social,

00:04:41.734 --> 00:04:45.033
as we learned during
a Trump rally in Ohio last week.

00:04:45.033 --> 00:04:48.434
-They conspired to ban me from
every social media platform

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:50.133
on the face of the Earth.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:51.968
Millions and millions of you

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:57.267
had already experienced
big tech's vicious censorship.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:59.667
Because of this digital tyranny,

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:02.300
we had to give the American
people their voice back

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.400
by building something
called "troth" --

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.033
"truth senchal."

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:10.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.200
-And it's just amazing.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.501
He got mad at Twitter
and made up his own version

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:16.667
out of pure vengeance,

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:17.934
and he can't even remember
what it's called.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.234
This is like if Darth Vader
was giving a speech

00:05:21.234 --> 00:05:24.334
to unveil the Death Star and
said, "[Crackles]

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:27.033
Soon, the universe
will bow to the Empire.

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.367
I give you the...

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:30.968
Kill Ball?

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:32.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:33.868
Death Ball?

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:35.467
Kevin?

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:36.934
Is Kevin back there?

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:38.901
What is it, again?

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:41.701
But it's not really a star,
though, is it, Kevin?

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:45.267
No, oh, no, I get it.

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:46.634
'Ball' is not great.

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:49.300
Thank you, Kevin."

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.968 --> 00:05:54.834
Also, could we just watch
that clip one more time?

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.534
-We had to give the American
people their voice back

00:05:57.534 --> 00:06:00.534
by building something
called "troth" --

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:02.300
"truth senchal."

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.567
-The best is in his head.

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:05.968
He's like, "I'm glad
I saved that 'troth' part."

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.400
"Stumbled on 'troth,'
but then got it back."

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:14.133
But, yeah, everyone should join

00:06:14.133 --> 00:06:17.567
Donald Trump's new social media
platform, Truth Central.

00:06:17.567 --> 00:06:20.868
Truth Central sounds like the
name of a law enforcement agency

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:23.901
in a dystopian sci-fi movie
where Tom Cruise arrests people

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:25.834
for crimes before they happen.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:27.934
Maybe that explains
why Rudy Giuliani always looks

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:30.634
like a precog who just woke up.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.634 --> 00:06:33.133
You don't have to be a precog...

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:35.701
to know we were gonna use
that picture of Rudy again.

00:06:35.701 --> 00:06:36.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:39.133
Let me save you
all the slime bath.

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:41.601
And maybe Trump's
inability to advertise

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:44.667
his own social media site
is hurting its success

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:47.701
because they're clearly
desperate for people to sign up.

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:50.133
On Tuesday, the C.E.O.
of Truth Social,

00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:51.834
former Congressman Devin Nunes,

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:54.234
perhaps
the world's only postcog,

00:06:54.234 --> 00:06:57.467
pleaded with the hosts of
"Fox &amp; Friends" to join the site

00:06:57.467 --> 00:07:00.834
and reveal their version
of the word "tweet is truth,"

00:07:00.834 --> 00:07:03.067
meaning that a post on the site
is known as a truth,

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:05.400
and posting a truth
is known as "truthing,"

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.033
which is, of course,
incredibly dumb

00:07:07.033 --> 00:07:10.634
and sounds even dumber
coming out of Nunes' mouth.

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:12.467
-We're so excited
that you're on Truth.

00:07:12.467 --> 00:07:14.133
You're getting followers
very, very quickly,

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:15.434
but you need to
send some truths out

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:17.100
if you want to get
more followers.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:20.467
But also, Brian, you're on
Truth, we need you to truth.

00:07:20.467 --> 00:07:23.300
But Doocy, I got to talk to him.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.033
So he's got to turn his phone on
and click on the app.

00:07:26.033 --> 00:07:27.400
He's been let in.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.100
-Every time you think
your life is bad, just remember,

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.467
you can be a former Congressman
begging Brian Kilmeade,

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:35.167
a man with the eyes of a Cabbage
Patch doll, to send out truths.

00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:37.334
Nunes sounds like
he should be in a phone booth,

00:07:37.334 --> 00:07:39.367
begging his bookie
to let him place one more bet.

00:07:39.367 --> 00:07:41.367
"Oh, come on, Ricky.
You know I'm good for it.

00:07:41.367 --> 00:07:42.801
I got a horse
who's a guaranteed winner!

00:07:42.801 --> 00:07:44.300
I want to put
a million bucks on him.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:45.968
They call him Truth.
Central Truth?

00:07:45.968 --> 00:07:47.234
No, wait, the Truth Star?

00:07:47.234 --> 00:07:48.634
Oh, God,
don't hang up on me, Ricky!

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:51.200
Ricky!"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.634
Nunes always looks like he
should be crying in his car

00:07:53.634 --> 00:07:55.534
in the parking lot
of Lumon Industries.

00:07:55.534 --> 00:07:58.200
That's our second reference
to "Severance,"

00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.701
the Apple TV show that has

00:07:59.701 --> 00:08:01.767
taken the "Late Night" offices
by storm.

00:08:01.767 --> 00:08:03.901
The first was on Monday,
and based on the response from

00:08:03.901 --> 00:08:06.100
the audience, it seemed like
not everyone was caught up.

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:08.167
But it's Wednesday now,
so to update us

00:08:08.167 --> 00:08:10.767
on where you are in regards
to "Severance," do please go to

00:08:10.767 --> 00:08:12.968
@seacaptainpolls on Twitter,

00:08:12.968 --> 00:08:15.267
where the options will be,
"yes, I'm caught up now,"

00:08:15.267 --> 00:08:16.701
"no, I'm still behind,"

00:08:16.701 --> 00:08:18.968
or "who the [bleep]
is the Sea Captain?"

00:08:18.968 --> 00:08:20.868
And just to show you
how bad the bugs are

00:08:20.868 --> 00:08:22.501
in Trump's Truth Social app,

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:25.767
later in the interview, Fox host
Steve Doocy did as instructed.

00:08:25.767 --> 00:08:28.367
He opened his phone
and told Nunes he was still

00:08:28.367 --> 00:08:30.000
in a waiting list
to join the app.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.367
-Congressman, I'm looking.

00:08:31.367 --> 00:08:34.067
I just signed on, and it says

00:08:34.067 --> 00:08:37.100
I have been created
successfully.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.701
"Due to massive demand, we have
placed you on a wait list."

00:08:39.701 --> 00:08:43.167
I'm number 621,000, still.

00:08:43.167 --> 00:08:44.434
-A waiting list?

00:08:44.434 --> 00:08:46.367
Isn't the whole point
of the Internet

00:08:46.367 --> 00:08:47.901
that everything is instant?

00:08:47.901 --> 00:08:49.868
This is like if
you clicked on Apple Maps

00:08:49.868 --> 00:08:52.801
and it was just a list of places
where you can buy a map.

00:08:52.801 --> 00:08:54.100
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:57.234
But even with their own social
media platform at stake,

00:08:57.234 --> 00:08:58.934
Trump, Nunes,
and their fellow Republicans

00:08:58.934 --> 00:09:00.400
are still celebrating the news

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:03.000
about Tesla and SpaceX C.E.O.
Elon Musk

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.534
finalizing a deal
to buy Twitter.

00:09:04.534 --> 00:09:05.634
And I have to say,

00:09:05.634 --> 00:09:07.300
it's certainly
an interesting decision

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:09.300
from a business perspective
to say the least,

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.567
given that Twitter
is not even profitable.

00:09:11.567 --> 00:09:13.834
-Elon Musk
is taking over Twitter

00:09:13.834 --> 00:09:16.767
to the tune of $44 billion.

00:09:16.767 --> 00:09:18.634
After weeks
of corporate wrangling,

00:09:18.634 --> 00:09:19.801
Twitter's board of directors

00:09:19.801 --> 00:09:22.167
accepting
the billionaire's buyout offer

00:09:22.167 --> 00:09:23.901
in a unanimous vote.

00:09:23.901 --> 00:09:26.133
-What do we know
about Elon Musk's plans

00:09:26.133 --> 00:09:27.901
to monetize Twitter,

00:09:27.901 --> 00:09:29.467
a company
that hasn't made a profit

00:09:29.467 --> 00:09:30.901
for 8 of the past 10 years?

00:09:30.901 --> 00:09:33.501
-One of the consistent issues
that Twitter has had

00:09:33.501 --> 00:09:34.834
for a very long time has been

00:09:34.834 --> 00:09:38.100
making this company
consistently profitable.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.334
And for a very long time,
that hasn't been the case.

00:09:40.334 --> 00:09:43.901
But I think this is really
more about ideology for Elon.

00:09:43.901 --> 00:09:46.667
-Musk has, according to him,

00:09:46.667 --> 00:09:52.767
raised about $13 billion
from Morgan Stanley.

00:09:52.767 --> 00:09:56.734
He's got another $12.5 billion

00:09:56.734 --> 00:10:01.167
he will help fund with loans
against his Tesla stock.

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:05.400
And he's adding $21 billion
of his own cash.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:06.767
-$44 billion?

00:10:06.767 --> 00:10:08.067
I mean, with money like that,

00:10:08.067 --> 00:10:10.467
you could do something about
poverty or climate change

00:10:10.467 --> 00:10:11.467
or world hunger

00:10:11.467 --> 00:10:13.000
and still have enough left over

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.100
to, I don't know,
get a decent haircut?

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:16.467
[ Laughter ]

00:10:16.467 --> 00:10:20.267
It looks like Tesla isn't
the only thing that uses plugs.

00:10:20.267 --> 00:10:23.801
Please don't kick me off
Twitter, Elon, please!

00:10:23.801 --> 00:10:27.267
It's the only place I can go
where people call me a cuck.

00:10:27.267 --> 00:10:29.334
I know it's a crazy thing to
like, but...

00:10:29.334 --> 00:10:32.234
classic cuck behavior, right?

00:10:32.234 --> 00:10:36.434
[ Laughter ]

00:10:36.434 --> 00:10:37.701
So, obviously,
there are potentially

00:10:37.701 --> 00:10:39.033
some really bad outcomes here.

00:10:39.033 --> 00:10:41.901
But regardless of whether
you're pro-Musk or anti-Musk,

00:10:41.901 --> 00:10:44.734
let's maybe
take a step back and reconsider

00:10:44.734 --> 00:10:47.334
whether it's a good thing
that everyone's just rooting

00:10:47.334 --> 00:10:49.300
for different billionaires
like sports teams,

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.334
which are also owned
by billionaires,

00:10:51.334 --> 00:10:53.067
a fact, I've been
reminded of repeatedly

00:10:53.067 --> 00:10:55.534
by my crew after
hedge-fund titan Steve Cohen

00:10:55.534 --> 00:10:58.167
bought the Mets, who now have
the most wins in baseball.

00:10:58.167 --> 00:11:00.767
And seeing how it's April,
that should hold up.

00:11:00.767 --> 00:11:03.400
[ Laughter ]

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:06.701
Famously, the Mets are in
October what they are in April.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.367
Yesterday, after the Mets won
their sixth series in a row,

00:11:10.367 --> 00:11:12.467
our security guard, Jim Bryer,
came up to me weeping

00:11:12.467 --> 00:11:14.100
and said, "This is
the greatest day of my life."

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.968
And then I asked him
what the second-best day was,

00:11:15.968 --> 00:11:17.400
and he said,
"When you got COVID."

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.467
Not cool, Jim.

00:11:18.467 --> 00:11:19.767
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.767 --> 00:11:21.434
Not cool.

00:11:21.434 --> 00:11:22.934
Not that I'd ever say that
to his face.

00:11:22.934 --> 00:11:24.334
I mean, look at the guy.

00:11:24.334 --> 00:11:26.367
I was talking to what I thought
was Jim for 20 minutes,

00:11:26.367 --> 00:11:28.601
and it turned out it was
just a rock in Central Park.

00:11:28.601 --> 00:11:32.200
[ Laughter ]

00:11:36.901 --> 00:11:38.367
[ Chuckles ]

00:11:38.367 --> 00:11:41.033
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:43.567
Maybe, just maybe, it's not
healthy for our democracy

00:11:43.567 --> 00:11:45.334
when Twitter, Facebook,
and "The Washington Post"

00:11:45.334 --> 00:11:48.000
are all owned by some of
the richest men in the world,

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.234
not to mention the fact that
Fox, "The Wall Street Journal,"

00:11:50.234 --> 00:11:52.767
and a network of right-wing
media outlets are owned

00:11:52.767 --> 00:11:54.067
by another
right-wing billionaire

00:11:54.067 --> 00:11:56.434
who's on the list of the
100 richest people in the world.

00:11:56.434 --> 00:11:57.367
That's not a free market.

00:11:57.367 --> 00:11:58.234
That's an oligarchy,

00:11:58.234 --> 00:11:59.434
which is why workers

00:11:59.434 --> 00:12:01.801
at major companies
like Amazon and Starbucks

00:12:01.801 --> 00:12:04.200
are trying to win back power
by unionizing,

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.868
a movement that's growing
stronger by the day.

00:12:05.868 --> 00:12:08.868
Bernie Sanders and A.O.C.
rallied with Amazon workers

00:12:08.868 --> 00:12:10.300
in Staten Island
over the weekend,

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.400
and Bernie recently took to
the Senate floor

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:14.868
to champion the reinvigorated
union movement,

00:12:14.868 --> 00:12:16.234
in typical Bernie fashion.

00:12:16.234 --> 00:12:18.968
-Unions provide better wages,

00:12:18.968 --> 00:12:24.467
benefits, and working conditions
for their members.

00:12:24.467 --> 00:12:26.601
That is what unions do.

00:12:26.601 --> 00:12:28.033
Not complicated.

00:12:28.033 --> 00:12:31.367
That is why it makes sense
to join a union

00:12:31.367 --> 00:12:33.200
and why it makes sense for us

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:35.033
to do everything that we can

00:12:35.033 --> 00:12:38.300
to grow the trade-union movement
in this country.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.300
And I know there are
some folks out there

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.400
who are not union members
and they're saying,

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:45.400
"Well, it doesn't really
impact me."

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:46.901
You're wrong. It does.

00:12:46.901 --> 00:12:48.901
-I love when Bernie cuts through
the bull[bleep].

00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:50.901
I wish they would have let him
host "Jeopardy!"

00:12:50.901 --> 00:12:53.300
"What is the Spanish Armada?"

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:54.367
"You're wrong."

00:12:54.367 --> 00:12:55.934
"Aren't you, um --

00:12:55.934 --> 00:12:58.634
Aren't you supposed to tell us
the right answer now?"

00:12:58.634 --> 00:13:01.033
"If you want to know
the right answers,

00:13:01.033 --> 00:13:02.634
you should have studied harder.

00:13:02.634 --> 00:13:06.834
Now pick a category,
or I'll pick it for you!"

00:13:06.834 --> 00:13:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:13:08.067 --> 00:13:11.133
No one knows how Musk's
acquisition of Twitter

00:13:11.133 --> 00:13:13.734
will turn out or whether Trump
will return to the platform

00:13:13.734 --> 00:13:15.234
and what the effect of that
will be.

00:13:15.234 --> 00:13:17.400
But one thing
we can know for sure

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.400
is that this much power
and wealth

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.968
in the hands of so few people
is definitely bad for democracy.

00:13:21.968 --> 00:13:24.767
We need a system that relies
less on the power of money

00:13:24.767 --> 00:13:25.834
and more on the...

00:13:25.834 --> 00:13:27.901
-♪ Power of love ♪

00:13:27.901 --> 00:13:31.968
[ Cheers and applause,
light laughter ]

00:13:31.968 --> 00:13:34.133
-When it barely got a reaction
the first time,

00:13:34.133 --> 00:13:36.267
did you think, "Oh, no,
that's our callback"?

00:13:36.267 --> 00:13:38.300
[ Laughter ]

00:13:39.901 --> 00:13:41.434
You know what this means, Sal?

00:13:41.434 --> 00:13:43.300
You know where you
and I have to go.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.334
Back to the future!

00:13:45.334 --> 00:13:47.067
[ Laughter ]

00:13:48.501 --> 00:13:50.634
"Don't do the
'Power of Love' joke!"

00:13:50.634 --> 00:13:53.267
[ Laughter ]

00:13:56.868 --> 00:13:58.367
Let's see, we did a little
Michael Caine.

00:13:58.367 --> 00:13:59.734
We got that in there.
Keith Richards.

00:13:59.734 --> 00:14:01.501
[ Muttering indistinctly ]
I think we got everything.

00:14:01.501 --> 00:14:02.667
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:14:02.667 --> 00:14:06.801
♪♪

00:14:06.801 --> 00:14:08.234
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:14:08.234 --> 00:14:10.534
over two million meals a year
to men, women, and children

00:14:10.534 --> 00:14:13.634
living with HIV/AIDS, cancer,
and other serious illness,

00:14:13.634 --> 00:14:15.534
and they need your help now
more than ever.

00:14:15.534 --> 00:14:17.701
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:14:17.701 --> 00:14:20.467
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

